I reviewed the diff by reading it and checking how `module-uast` is used. I did not re-run any suites, as instructed.

**1. Install/deliver split: sound.**
- `module-uast` (`safepoint.cljc:249-259`) now conj's `(require (quote py))` after the hook definitions. It is the last operand, so every `def!` still precedes every call, including the `require`. That keeps the sibling-read discharge intact.
- The install defines hooks and requires `py` only. It never calls `py/init!`.
- The docstring says the same.
- `module-spec` derives its free names from `module-uast` (`safepoint.cljc:270-276`), and `:requires` is `{py py-address}` (`safepoint.cljc:~285`), so the require and its pin come from one source.
- The new `pysp-manifest-address` golden (`cf017bd4…`) moves because the module tree changed. The test docstring records why.
